{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce5C3Df1beAM6rcZh3isx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I take this as the Eastgate Park & Ride in Bellevue, Washington — tell me if you mean a different Eastgate (Cincinnati and Chattanooga also have one, but neither has a garage as far as I know).\n\n**What it is**\n- A King County Metro park-and-ride at about 14200 SE Eastgate Way, Bellevue, just south of I-90 near the Bellevue College exit.\n- It is one of the larger park-and-rides on the Eastside. The site combines a multi-level garage with surface stalls, for roughly 1,600 spaces in total.\n- The lot fills early on weekdays. Historically it was at or above capacity before 8:00 a.m.\n\n**Transit service**\n- A direct-access ramp connects the freeway station to the I-90 HOV lanes, so buses enter and leave without using the general-purpose lanes.\n- Metro routes serve Bellevue, Issaquah, Bellevue College, and Seattle from here. Sound Transit route 554 (Issaquah–Seattle corridor) has also used the freeway station.\n- Eastgate is **not** a light rail station. The 2 Line turns north at Bellevue Way, so Eastgate stays a bus hub.\n\n**Caveats**\n- Route numbers, service patterns, and permit-parking rules on the Eastside changed several times around the 2 Line openings and the Metro restructures. My knowledge stops in May 2026, so treat the service details above as approximate.\n- I did not verify any of this against a live source in this session.\n\nWant me to look up the current stall count, route list, and permit rules from Metro and Sound Transit?"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15052,"cache_read_input_tokens":18898,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15052},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_